of strings-en-gb.xml; CI checks that none is missing.

The first group is GOV.UK's own wording, taken unchanged from the Government
Digital Service's govuk_publishing_components (config/locales/es.yml at
commit 7f411f2), (c) Crown Copyright (Government Digital Service), MIT licence;
see NOTICE.md in this folder. The second group is this project's translation,
for text GOV.UK has no wording for.

The toolkit labels the plugin's pages show are given here too, under the
toolkit's own ids and with DITA-OT's own Spanish wording where it has one,
so that every Spanish locale registered in strings.xml reads the same
whether or not DITA-OT has strings for it.
-->
